WEBVTT

00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:10,350
What do you think about

00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:14,230
deuterium related to illness and disease

00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:18,670
and can deuterium depletion help us?

00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:20,510
Wow, good question.

00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:25,510
So deuterium is oxygen with an extra hydrogen on it.

00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:31,150
And deuterium is in all of our water supply.

00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:34,470
A percentage of our water is deuterium.

00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:40,310
They're really interesting studies on deuterium.

00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:45,310
Societies, or you could say cultures,

00:00:45,310 --> 00:00:50,310
that drink water that has less deuterium in it,

00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:52,990
live longer across the board.

00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:55,470
They live longer.

00:00:57,310 --> 00:00:58,150
Why is that?

00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:01,910
Deuterium is heavy water, it's called heavy water.

00:01:01,910 --> 00:01:06,830
And it doesn't function in our body as water.

00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:10,510
And it can block water's function in our body.

00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:14,790
So you can actually buy deuterium depleted water.

00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:17,790
So what are the societies that drink water?

00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:21,310
Where is water that has less deuterium in it?

00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:24,830
Every all of our water throughout this entire planet

00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:25,990
has deuterium in it.

00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:29,430
But there's some water that has less deuterium in it.

00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:33,990
And that is water that's melted from glacial water.

00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:39,990
There is a bottled water company called Icelandic.

00:01:39,990 --> 00:01:41,830
You've heard of Icelandic water.

00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:43,910
They might sell it in the grocery store.

00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:46,430
They might sell it at a gas station.

00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:51,430
Comes in a kind of a square bottle with ridges on it.

00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:56,670
It is naturally deuterium depleted water.

00:01:56,670 --> 00:01:59,910
It has a lower content of deuterium in it.

00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:04,150
And really, there can be benefits to drinking Icelandic water.

00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:07,110
So deuterium depleted water, you could actually buy.

00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:11,550
There's a process where you could deplete deuterium in the water.

00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:13,990
It's just quite expensive.

00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:17,910
And there's been studies where people have used deuterium depleted water

00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:19,190
with cancer.

00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:22,150
And some that people have gotten better

00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:24,470
just using deuterium depleted water.

00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:27,430
It can't be difficult to get.

00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:31,230
You have to order it, I think from overseas.

00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:33,950
I don't think there's a place in the US that makes it.

00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:39,510
But it's, but you can get slightly deuterium depleted water

00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:41,390
with Icelandic water.

00:02:41,390 --> 00:02:43,750
That's one thing I did talk about.

00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:46,190
What do you do with your cancer?

00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:49,430
What about a bug I drank Icelandic water?

00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:52,270
And then we had it on order.

00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:53,750
You could order it on Amazon.

00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,590
We had it just out of delivery.

00:02:55,590 --> 00:02:58,910
So probably a couple of months that we were drinking Icelandic,

00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:00,790
which is slightly deuterium depleted water.

00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:03,230
I don't remember the numbers of the scale.

00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:04,630
I'd have to look that up.

00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:06,630
But there can be benefits to deuterium

00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:09,630
both depleted water sources.

